# maskfromcurves

- Label: Mask from Curves
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 12 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/maskfromcurves.html
- Summary (EN): The Mask from Curves node closes 2D curves and renders them into a black-and-white mask. It can also output a signed distance field (SDF) storing each pixel distance to the curves.
- Résumé (FR) : Ferme des courbes 2D et les rend en masque noir et blanc, ou en champ de distance signée qui indique la distance de chaque pixel aux courbes.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: layer onto which the curves are rendered; if the curves are not on this layer they are projected through its camera", "curves: geometry containing the curves to rasterise; open curves are closed first"]

- Key parameters: ["Output Type: Mask (white inside, black outside) or SDF", "Invert: reverses inside and outside in the mask or SDF output, without changing id values", "Blur: postprocess blur softening the mask edges", "Units: blur Size in image space or absolute pixels", "Conversion Quality: smoothness of NURBS and Bezier conversion to polygons, at the cost of processing time", "Resample / Segment Length: resamples incoming polygons to equal-spaced points using the given world-space segment length", "Treat Polygons As: Straight Edges, Subdivision Curves or Interpolating Curves when resampling"]

- Caveats: ["Polygon, Bezier and NURBS curves are accepted; non-polygon curves are converted automatically", "The id output stores the contributing curve number per pixel, with -1 where no curve contributed", "With Blur enabled, the mask can be non-zero in pixels that have no id", "Interpolating Curves preserve size but can introduce overshoots and oscillations", "Documented as available since version 21.0"]

